{
  "title": "Perfect tense and principal parts",
  "note": "The perfect tells what happened or has happened: amavi, I loved or have loved. Its endings are -i, -isti, -it, -imus, -istis, -erunt. Its stem is the third principal part and must be learned with each verb: amo, amare, amavi; video, videre, vidi; venio, venire, veni. Veni, vidi, vici: I came, I saw, I conquered.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, The Perfect Stem",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/perfect-stem"
  },
